# uSDXn V1

A simple, buildable, open-source QRP SDR transceiver for 40 meters.

## About uSDXn

uSDXn is an open-source and open-hardware QRP SDR transceiver project focused on simplicity, accessibility, experimentation, education, and home construction.

The project is developed with a modular approach, separating the main functional areas of the transceiver so they can be studied, modified, tested, and developed independently.

uSDXn V1 is the first hardware release of the uSDXn project.

## Relationship to uSDX

uSDXn is based on the uSDX concept and builds upon the work of Guido PE1NNZ and contributors to the original uSDX project.

The original uSDX project and its software remain credited to their respective authors and contributors.

uSDXn V1 is an independent hardware development based on the uSDX concept, developed for experimentation, education, and further community development.

### Original uSDX

Original uSDX project by Guido PE1NNZ and contributors.

